From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabricio Akio <fabricioakio@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 14:18:18 -0300
Subject: power: supply: pmi8998_fg: release the charger reference

power_supply_get_by_reference() takes a reference on the charger that
the driver never puts. Use the managed variant, which puts it when the
driver is unbound.

Signed-off-by: Fabricio Akio <fabricioakio@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c b/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c
@@ -654,8 +654,8 @@ static int pmi8998_fg_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	}
 
 	/* Optional: Get charger power supply for status checking */
-	chip->chg_psy = power_supply_get_by_reference(dev_fwnode(chip->dev),
-						    "power-supplies");
+	chip->chg_psy = devm_power_supply_get_by_reference(chip->dev,
+							   "power-supplies");
 	if (IS_ERR(chip->chg_psy)) {
 		ret = PTR_ERR(chip->chg_psy);
 		dev_warn(chip->dev, "Failed to get charger supply: %d\n", ret);
-- 
Armbian

